             <div class="blog-content">
                 <div class="blog-body">
                     <h1 class="blog-title">Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 Link – Check Your Inter Results Online Now!</h1>

                     <p>The wait is almost over for lakhs of students who appeared for the Bihar Board Intermediate (Class 12) examinations in 2026! The Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB) is gearing up to declare the much-anticipated Class 12 results, a pivotal moment that will shape the academic and career paths of countless students across the state. This comprehensive guide will walk you through everything you need to know about checking your BSEB 12th Result 2026 online, including expected release dates, official links, and crucial details.</p>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Expected Release Date for BSEB 12th Result 2026</h2>
                     <p>The Bihar Board 12th exams for 2026 were conducted from February 2 to February 13, 2026. Following past trends, the BSEB Class 12 results are typically announced in March. This year, multiple reports and official statements indicate that the Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 is expected to be declared between <strong>March 20 and March 25, 2026</strong>. Some sources even suggest a specific announcement time of <strong>11:00 AM on March 23, 2026</strong>.</p>
                     <p>The board concludes various steps, including answer sheet evaluation and topper verification, before the official announcement. Topper verification is a crucial final stage to ensure accuracy and fairness in the results.</p>

                     <div class="highlight-text">
                         Students are advised to keep their admit cards handy as they will need their Roll Code and Roll Number to access their results.
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Official Websites to Check Your Inter Result</h2>
                     <p>To ensure you access your results safely and accurately, it is critical to rely only on the official websites provided by the Bihar School Examination Board. Here are the primary official portals where you can check your BSEB 12th Result 2026:</p>
                     <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                         <p>✅ <a href="https://biharboardonline.bihar.gov.in/" target="_blank">biharboardonline.bihar.gov.in</a></p>
                         <p>✅ <a href="https://results.biharboardonline.com/" target="_blank">results.biharboardonline.com</a></p>
                         <p>✅ <a href="https://interbiharboard.com/" target="_blank">interbiharboard.com</a></p>
                         <p>✅ <a href="https://interresult2026.com/" target="_blank">interresult2026.com</a></p>
                         <p>You can also check your results on DigiLocker once they are officially released.</p>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Step-by-Step Guide: How to Check Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 Online</h2>
                     <p>Follow these simple steps to easily check and download your Bihar Board Intermediate Result 2026 once it is declared:</p>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit an Official Website</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Open your web browser and go to any of the official BSEB result portals mentioned above.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the link that says "Bihar Board 12th Result 2026," "Intermediate Annual Examination 2026 Result," or similar. Click on it.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a login page. Here, carefully enter your Roll Code and Roll Number exactly as they appear on your Bihar Board 12th Admit Card. Some portals might also ask for your Date of Birth.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">4. Submit and View Result</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">After entering the required details, click on the "Submit," "View Result," or "Search" button. Your Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 will be displayed on your screen.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">5. Download and Print Marksheet</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Review your subject-wise marks, total score, division, and pass/fail status. It is highly recommended to download and save a digital copy of your provisional marksheet and take a printout for future reference. This digital copy will be essential for college admissions and other official purposes until original certificates are issued by your school.</div>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Details Mentioned on Your Online Marksheet</h2>
                     <p>Your provisional online marksheet for the BSEB 12th Result 2026 will contain several important details. Make sure to cross-check all the information carefully:</p>
                     <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                         <p>✅ Student's Name</p>
                         <p>✅ Roll Code and Roll Number</p>
                         <p>✅ Stream (Science, Commerce, Arts)</p>
                         <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks</p>
                         <p>✅ Total Marks Obtained</p>
                         <p>✅ Division Secured</p>
                         <p>✅ Pass/Fail Status</p>
                         <p>✅ Other relevant grades or remarks</p>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Passing Criteria for Bihar Board Class 12 Exams</h2>
                     <p>To successfully pass the BSEB Class 12 examinations, students must meet the following criteria:</p>
                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">Minimum Marks Required</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Students need to score at least 30% to 33% marks in each theory subject. For subjects that include practical examinations, a minimum of 40% marks is required in the practical component, and it is necessary to pass both theory and practical exams separately.</div>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Bihar Board 12th Result: Past Year Trends</h2>
                     <p>Understanding the result declaration patterns from previous years can give students an idea of the consistency of BSEB's timelines. The board consistently releases Intermediate results in March.</p>
                     <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                         <thead>
                             <tr>
                                 <th>Year</th>
                                 <th>Bihar Board 12th Result Date</th>
                                 <th>Approx. Pass Percentage</th>
                             </tr>
                         </thead>
                         <tbody>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>2026 (Expected)</td>
                                 <td>March 20-25</td>
                                 <td>-</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>2025</td>
                                 <td>March 25</td>
                                 <td>86.56%</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>2024</td>
                                 <td>March 23</td>
                                 <td>-</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>2023</td>
                                 <td>March 21</td>
                                 <td>-</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>2022</td>
                                 <td>March 16</td>
                                 <td>-</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>2021</td>
                                 <td>March 26</td>
                                 <td>-</td>
                             </tr>
                         </tbody>
                     </table>
                     <p>In 2025, Commerce stream recorded the highest pass rate at 94.77%, followed by Science at 89.66% and Arts at 82.75%. Top scorers in previous years have achieved marks in the high 90s.</p>

                     <h2 class="section-title">What After the Results?</h2>
                     <p>Once the Bihar Board 12th results are out, students can plan their next steps for higher education. The provisional marksheet can be used for college admissions, scholarship applications, and entrance exams. Remember that the original certificates will be issued by your respective schools a few days after the online declaration.</p>
                     <p>For top performers, the BSEB also awards cash prizes and recognition on "Medha Diwas."</p>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">Q1: When is the Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 expected?</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">The Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 is expected to be declared between March 20 and March 25, 2026. Some reports indicate March 23, 2026, at 11:00 AM.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">Q2: What details are required to check the BSEB 12th Result?</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">You will need your Roll Code and Roll Number, found on your admit card, to check your Bihar Board 12th Result 2026. Some websites may also ask for your Date of Birth.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">Q3: Where can I find the official links for Bihar Board 12th Result 2026?</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">The official websites are biharboardonline.bihar.gov.in, results.biharboardonline.com, interbiharboard.com, and interresult2026.com.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">Q4: Will the original marksheet be available online?</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">The online marksheet you download will be provisional. Original certificates and marksheets will be distributed by your respective schools a few days after the online result declaration.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">Q5: What are the passing marks for Bihar Board Class 12 exams?</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Students must score a minimum of 30-33% in each theory subject and 40% in practical subjects to pass.</div>
                     </div>

                     <p>We wish all the students awaiting their Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 the very best of luck! Stay calm, follow the official channels, and celebrate your hard-earned success.</p>

